            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it exactly the same and it was delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-02T17:53:04.270Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jbooshey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this as a sandwich spread like another reviewer suggested. I cooked some seasoned chicken breast and sliced it. Then I pan toasted some sourdough, put the chicken on it with sliced of provolone. Then added lettuce and onion with the spread and yum yum.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-14T11:22:53.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BigShotsMom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a hit in my house. I puréed the sun dried tomatoes to get a smooth consistency and used dry basil. As I filled the dish for the second time I realized I had forgotten the lemon juice so I added a bit. It helped cut the richness but it was fine without it. Thanks, Terry!",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-23T18:06:19.193Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Holiday Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this yesterday for a snack dip. I mixed up 1/3 of the recipe and got about 1/2 cup of dip. After I made it, I realized I forgot the lemon juice. However, it tasted fine. For the fresh basil I used 1 tsp. of dried as a subtitute. I used lite mayo and sour cream with no problems. I wasn't sure what would be good to dip with. I used some pretzels and that was tasty. The dip looked somewhat like the classic vegetable dips but had a very slight pizza after taste with pretzels.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-21T05:19:11.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LISAREC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is so good! I spread it on panini sandwiches with grilled chicken &amp; provolone cheese! Yummy! Mixed it all in my mini food processor. We also didn't let it sit for an hour. We served it right away &amp; it was awesome!",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-07T11:14:36.380Z"
          },
          {
